 const notes=[
 ["1. Cell, tissue and body organisation","The cell is the basic structural and functional unit. Cell membranes regulate movement of substances; mitochondria generate ATP; ribosomes synthesise proteins; the nucleus stores genetic material. The four basic tissue groups are epithelial, connective, muscle and nervous tissue. Connective tissue includes bone, cartilage, blood, tendons and ligaments. Understanding tissue structure helps explain injury, healing and organ function.","कोषिका शरीरको आधारभूत संरचनात्मक र कार्यात्मक एकाइ हो। Cell membrane ले पदार्थको आवतजावत नियन्त्रण गर्छ; mitochondria ले ATP बनाउँछ; ribosome ले protein बनाउँछ र nucleus मा genetic material हुन्छ। मुख्य tissue चार प्रकारका हुन्छन्: epithelial, connective, muscle र nervous tissue।"],
 ["2. Bone, joints and muscular system","The skeleton supports and protects organs, provides leverage for movement and stores minerals. Long, short, flat and irregular bones have different shapes. Joints may be fibrous, cartilaginous or synovial. Skeletal muscle produces voluntary movement; smooth muscle acts in hollow organs and cardiac muscle pumps blood. Anaesthesia positioning must protect joints, pressure points and peripheral nerves.","हड्डीले शरीरलाई आधार, अंगलाई सुरक्षा, movement का लागि leverage र mineral भण्डारण दिन्छ। Joint fibrous, cartilaginous वा synovial हुन सक्छ। Skeletal muscle ले इच्छाअनुसार movement गर्छ; smooth muscle भित्री अंगमा र cardiac muscle मुटुमा काम गर्छ। Anaesthesia समयमा position मिलाउँदा joint, pressure point र nerve जोगाउनुपर्छ।"],
 ["3. Blood, haemoglobin and red-cell indices","Blood contains plasma, erythrocytes, leukocytes and platelets. Haemoglobin carries oxygen. PCV/haematocrit is the proportion of blood volume occupied by red cells; ESR is a non-specific marker influenced by plasma proteins and red-cell properties. MCV estimates average red-cell volume, MCH average haemoglobin per cell and MCHC average haemoglobin concentration. Interpret these with the blood film and clinical context.","रगतमा plasma, RBC, WBC र platelet हुन्छन्। Haemoglobin ले oxygen बोक्छ। PCV ले रगतमा RBC ले ओगटेको आयतन जनाउँछ; ESR plasma protein र RBC को अवस्थाबाट प्रभावित हुने non-specific सूचक हो। MCV, MCH र MCHC ले RBC को आकार तथा haemoglobin सम्बन्धी सूचक दिन्छन्।"],
 ["4. Haemostasis, blood groups and transfusion basics","Haemostasis limits bleeding through vascular response, platelet plug formation and coagulation. ABO and RhD are clinically important blood-group systems. Before transfusion, verify patient and component identity, perform required compatibility testing and follow local blood-bank policy. Acute transfusion reaction: stop the transfusion, maintain IV access with compatible fluid under protocol, assess the patient, notify the clinical team and blood bank, and send required samples.","Haemostasis ले रक्तनलीको प्रतिक्रिया, platelet plug र coagulation मार्फत रक्तस्राव रोक्छ। ABO र RhD महत्त्वपूर्ण blood-group system हुन्। Transfusion अघि बिरामी र blood component पहिचान, compatibility test र blood-bank policy पालना गर्नुपर्छ। Reaction शंका भए transfusion रोक्ने, protocol अनुसार IV access कायम राख्ने, बिरामी जाँच्ने र clinical team तथा blood bank लाई खबर गर्ने।"],
 ["5. Cardiovascular and respiratory physiology","The right heart pumps blood to the lungs; the left heart pumps oxygenated blood to systemic circulation. Cardiac output equals heart rate multiplied by stroke volume. Ventilation moves air; diffusion exchanges gases across the alveolar-capillary membrane; perfusion delivers blood to the lungs. Oxygenation depends on ventilation, diffusion, perfusion, haemoglobin and circulation.","दायाँ मुटुले फोक्सोमा र बायाँ मुटुले oxygen भएको रगत शरीरमा पठाउँछ। Cardiac output = heart rate × stroke volume हो। Ventilation ले हावा चलाउँछ, diffusion ले alveoli र capillary बीच gas साट्छ र perfusion ले फोक्सोमा रगत पुर्‍याउँछ। Oxygenation मा ventilation, diffusion, perfusion, haemoglobin र circulation सबै महत्त्वपूर्ण हुन्छन्।"],
 ["6. Gastrointestinal, urinary and endocrine systems","The gastrointestinal tract digests and absorbs nutrients. The liver metabolises nutrients, produces bile and synthesises many plasma proteins; the pancreas has digestive and endocrine functions. Kidneys regulate fluid, electrolytes and acid–base balance and excrete waste. Endocrine glands release hormones into blood; insulin lowers glucose, while thyroid and adrenal hormones influence metabolism and stress responses.","पाचन प्रणालीले खाना पचाएर पोषक तत्व सोस्छ। Liver ले nutrient metabolism, bile उत्पादन र plasma protein synthesis गर्छ; pancreas को digestive र endocrine दुवै काम हुन्छ। मिर्गौलाले पानी, electrolyte र acid–base सन्तुलन मिलाउँछ। Endocrine gland ले hormone रगतमा छोड्छ।"],
 ["7. Nervous system, sensory organs and embryology","The central nervous system comprises brain and spinal cord; the peripheral nervous system connects the CNS with the body. Autonomic pathways regulate involuntary functions: sympathetic activity supports stress responses and parasympathetic activity supports restorative functions. Sensory organs detect light, sound, balance, taste and smell. Embryology describes development from fertilisation through organ formation; developmental abnormalities may affect airway, heart and other systems.","Central nervous system मा brain र spinal cord पर्छन्; peripheral nervous system ले CNS लाई शरीरसँग जोड्छ। Autonomic nervous system ले अनैच्छिक काम नियन्त्रण गर्छ। Sensory organ ले प्रकाश, आवाज, सन्तुलन, स्वाद र गन्ध पहिचान गर्छ। Embryology ले fertilisation देखि अंग विकाससम्मको प्रक्रिया अध्ययन गर्छ।"],
 ["8. Carbohydrates, lipids, proteins and nucleic acids","Carbohydrates are a major energy source; lipids provide energy storage, cell membranes and steroid precursors; proteins provide structure, enzymes, transport and immune functions. Digestion breaks macromolecules into absorbable units. Nucleotides form DNA and RNA, which store and express genetic information. Metabolic pathways are regulated by enzymes and hormones.","Carbohydrate मुख्य ऊर्जा स्रोत हो; lipid ले ऊर्जा भण्डारण, cell membrane र steroid precursor दिन्छ; protein ले संरचना, enzyme, transport र immunity मा काम गर्छ। पाचनले ठूला अणुलाई सोस्न मिल्ने साना एकाइमा तोड्छ। Nucleotide ले DNA र RNA बनाउँछ।"],
 ["9. Enzymes, vitamins, minerals and nutrition","Enzymes are biological catalysts whose activity depends on temperature, pH, substrate concentration and inhibitors. Vitamins and minerals are needed for metabolism, blood formation, bone health, nerve function and coagulation; both deficiency and excess can cause disease. A balanced diet supplies adequate energy and essential nutrients. BMR is energy used at rest; dietary fibre supports bowel health. Malnutrition includes undernutrition and overnutrition.","Enzyme जैविक catalyst हो; यसको काम तापक्रम, pH, substrate र inhibitor बाट प्रभावित हुन्छ। Vitamin र mineral metabolism, रक्तनिर्माण, हड्डी, nerve र coagulation का लागि चाहिन्छन्; कमी र बढी दुवैले रोग गराउन सक्छ। सन्तुलित आहारले ऊर्जा र पोषक तत्व दिन्छ। BMR आराममा खर्च हुने ऊर्जा हो; fibre ले आन्द्राको स्वास्थ्यमा मद्दत गर्छ।"],
 ["10. Acid–base balance and clinical biochemistry","pH reflects hydrogen-ion activity; buffers resist abrupt pH change. The bicarbonate–carbon dioxide system is central to blood pH regulation. The Henderson–Hasselbalch equation relates pH to bicarbonate and dissolved CO2. Acidosis is a process tending to lower pH; alkalosis tends to raise it. Respiratory disorders primarily alter CO2, while metabolic disorders primarily alter bicarbonate. Interpret blood gases with clinical status and compensation.","pH ले hydrogen-ion activity जनाउँछ; buffer ले pH को अचानक परिवर्तन रोक्छ। Bicarbonate–CO2 प्रणाली रगतको pH नियन्त्रणमा मुख्य हुन्छ। Acidosis ले pH घटाउने र alkalosis ले बढाउने प्रक्रिया हो। Respiratory समस्या मुख्यतः CO2 र metabolic समस्या मुख्यतः bicarbonate मा देखिन्छ।"],
 ["11. Renal function and serum analytes","Glucose, proteins, urea, uric acid, creatinine, bilirubin, cholesterol and electrolytes are interpreted using validated reference intervals. Creatinine and estimated filtration measures help assess renal function; urea is influenced by hydration, protein intake and catabolism. Electrolyte abnormalities can affect cardiac rhythm, muscle function and consciousness. Check sample quality and clinical context before interpreting results.","Glucose, protein, urea, uric acid, creatinine, bilirubin, cholesterol र electrolyte लाई प्रयोगशालाको reference interval अनुसार व्याख्या गर्नुपर्छ। Creatinine र filtration estimate ले मिर्गौलाको कार्य बुझ्न मद्दत गर्छ। Electrolyte गडबडीले मुटुको rhythm, muscle र चेतनामा असर गर्न सक्छ।"],
 ["12. Haematology tests and anticoagulants","Collect blood using the correct tube and fill volume. EDTA is commonly used for complete blood count; citrate is used for coagulation testing at the correct blood-to-anticoagulant ratio; other additives are selected for specific chemistry tests. Haemoglobin can be measured by validated laboratory methods. PT assesses the extrinsic and common pathways; aPTT assesses intrinsic and common pathways. BT and CT are older screening tests and should be interpreted according to local practice.","सही tube र उचित मात्रामा रगत संकलन गर्नुपर्छ। CBC मा EDTA, coagulation मा सही अनुपातको citrate र अन्य chemistry मा परीक्षणअनुसार additive प्रयोग हुन्छ। PT ले extrinsic/common र aPTT ले intrinsic/common pathway मूल्याङ्कन गर्छ। BT र CT पुराना screening test हुन्; स्थानीय practice अनुसार व्याख्या गर्नुपर्छ।"],
 ["13. Blood bank and transfusion safety","Donated blood is collected, identified, screened, processed and stored under regulated conditions. Compatibility testing reduces risk but does not remove all transfusion risk. Reactions may be acute or delayed and can be immune or non-immune. Watch for fever, chills, rash, dyspnoea, hypotension, pain or dark urine. Stop transfusion and follow the institution's reaction protocol immediately.","दान गरिएको रगत पहिचान, screening, processing र नियन्त्रित अवस्थामा भण्डारण गरिन्छ। Compatibility testing ले जोखिम घटाउँछ तर पूर्ण हटाउँदैन। Reaction acute वा delayed तथा immune वा non-immune हुन सक्छ। ज्वरो, कम्पन, rash, सास कष्ट, hypotension, दुखाइ वा गाढा पिसाब देखिए transfusion रोक्दै protocol पालना गर्नुपर्छ।"],
 ["14. Microbiology, infection and sterilisation","Bacteria require suitable nutrients, temperature, pH and atmosphere. Culture media are selected for the organism and purpose. Sterilisation destroys all forms of microbial life; disinfection reduces pathogenic organisms but may not destroy spores. Infection prevention includes hand hygiene, PPE, aseptic technique, safe sharps disposal and biomedical-waste segregation at source. Immunology explains antigen recognition and host defence.","ब्याक्टेरियालाई उपयुक्त पोषक तत्व, तापक्रम, pH र वातावरण चाहिन्छ। जीव र उद्देश्यअनुसार culture media छानिन्छ। Sterilisation ले सबै प्रकारका सूक्ष्मजीव नष्ट गर्छ; disinfection ले रोगजनक घटाउँछ तर spore नष्ट नहुन सक्छ। संक्रमण रोकथाममा hand hygiene, PPE, aseptic technique र waste segregation पर्छ।"],
 ["15. Clinical specimen handling and body fluids","Specimen quality begins with correct patient identification, correct container, appropriate collection, prompt transport and suitable preservation. Urine is examined physically, chemically and microscopically. CSF requires urgent handling when meningitis is suspected. Sputum should be a lower-respiratory specimen rather than saliva where possible. Stool examination may include macroscopic and microscopic assessment. Label at collection and document time and source.","नमुनाको गुणस्तर सही बिरामी पहिचान, container, संकलन, छिटो ढुवानी र संरक्षणमा निर्भर हुन्छ। Urine physical, chemical र microscopic रूपमा जाँचिन्छ। Meningitis शंका हुँदा CSF छिटो प्रयोगशालामा पुर्‍याउनुपर्छ। Sputum सकेसम्म तल्लो श्वासप्रश्वासबाट आएको हुनुपर्छ।"],
 ["16. Applied pathology: cardiovascular and blood disorders","Atherosclerosis involves lipid-rich plaque in arterial walls and contributes to ischaemic heart disease. Hypertension damages target organs; aneurysm is abnormal vessel dilatation. Valvular disease and cardiomyopathy impair cardiac function; pericardial effusion may impair filling and cause tamponade. Congenital heart disease results from developmental defects. Anaemia is reduced oxygen-carrying capacity; leukocyte disorders include leukocytosis, agranulocytosis and leukaemia; bleeding disorders require clinical and laboratory assessment.","Atherosclerosis मा धमनीको भित्तामा lipid plaque बन्छ र IHD हुन सक्छ। Hypertension ले अंगमा क्षति पुर्‍याउँछ; aneurysm रक्तनली असामान्य फैलिनु हो। Valve रोग, cardiomyopathy र pericardial effusion ले मुटुको काम बिगार्न सक्छ। Anaemia मा oxygen बोक्ने क्षमता घट्छ; WBC रोगमा leukocytosis, agranulocytosis र leukaemia पर्छन्।"],
 ["17. Applied pathology: respiratory and renal disorders","COPD includes chronic obstructive airway disease such as chronic bronchitis and emphysema. Obstructive disease limits airflow; restrictive disease reduces lung expansion/volume. Pneumoconiosis follows inhalation of certain dusts. Pulmonary congestion/oedema and pleural effusion impair gas exchange. Acute and chronic renal failure cause fluid, electrolyte and waste-retention problems. Glomerulonephritis affects glomeruli; pyelonephritis affects kidney tissue and pelvis. ESRD may require dialysis or transplantation.","COPD मा chronic bronchitis र emphysema जस्ता obstructive airway रोग पर्छन्। Obstructive रोगले airflow र restrictive रोगले फोक्सो फैलिने क्षमता घटाउँछ। धुलोको असरबाट pneumoconiosis हुन सक्छ। Renal failure मा पानी, electrolyte र waste जम्मा हुन्छ। ESRD मा dialysis वा transplant आवश्यक हुन सक्छ।"],
 ["18. Pharmacokinetics, pharmacodynamics and safe medication practice","Pharmacokinetics describes absorption, distribution, metabolism and excretion; pharmacodynamics describes what a drug does to the body, including receptor action and dose-response. Dose and route depend on indication, age, weight, organ function, interactions and monitoring. Check the prescription, allergies, concentration, calculation, route and patient identity. Drug doses in anaesthesia are high-risk and must follow current institutional protocols and authorised supervision.","Pharmacokinetics मा absorption, distribution, metabolism र excretion पर्छ; pharmacodynamics ले औषधिले शरीरमा गर्ने प्रभाव बताउँछ। मात्रा र route रोग, उमेर, तौल, अंगको कार्य, interaction र monitoring अनुसार हुन्छ। Prescription, allergy, concentration, calculation, route र पहिचान जाँच्नुहोस्। Anaesthesia औषधिको dose उच्च जोखिमयुक्त हुन्छ र हालको protocol तथा अधिकृत supervision पालना गर्नुपर्छ।"],
 ["19. Autonomic and cardiovascular pharmacology","The sympathetic system generally supports fight-or-flight responses; the parasympathetic system supports rest-and-digest functions. Drugs acting on adrenergic or cholinergic receptors may alter heart rate, vascular tone, airway calibre and secretions. Cardiovascular groups in the syllabus include beta/alpha blockers, vasodilators, calcium-channel blockers, antiarrhythmics, cardiac glycosides, inotropes, anti-anginals, heart-failure drugs and lipid-lowering agents. Learn each drug's action, indications, contraindications and adverse effects from current references.","Sympathetic system ले stress response र parasympathetic ले rest-and-digest काममा सहयोग गर्छ। Adrenergic वा cholinergic receptor मा काम गर्ने औषधिले heart rate, रक्तनली, airway र secretion बदल्न सक्छ। Syllabus मा beta/alpha blocker, vasodilator, calcium-channel blocker, antiarrhythmic, cardiac glycoside, inotrope र अन्य cardiovascular drug समूह छन्।"],
 ["20. Anaesthetic, analgesic and emergency pharmacology","Anaesthetic agents may be inhalational or intravenous and produce hypnosis, amnesia, analgesia or immobility in different combinations. Opioids provide analgesia but may depress respiration. Neuromuscular blockers cause paralysis and do not provide unconsciousness or analgesia. Reversal agents and monitoring are essential. Emergency medicines and doses depend on the clinical event, patient factors and current protocol; never rely on memory alone for administration.","Anaesthetic agent inhalational वा intravenous हुन सक्छ र hypnosis, amnesia, analgesia वा immobility फरक संयोजनमा दिन्छ। Opioid ले दुखाइ घटाउँछ तर श्वास दबाउन सक्छ। Neuromuscular blocker ले paralysis गर्छ, बेहोस वा analgesia दिँदैन। Reversal र monitoring आवश्यक हुन्छ। Emergency drug र dose अवस्था तथा protocol अनुसार हुन्छ।"],
 ["21. Anaesthesia machine, gases and breathing systems","The anaesthesia workstation supplies medical gases, controls flow, delivers volatile agent through a vaporiser when used, and connects to a breathing system and scavenging. Check pipeline and cylinder supply, pressure, flowmeters, oxygen analyser, alarms, vapouriser seating/fill, breathing circuit integrity, leak test and ventilator function according to the machine checklist. Oxygen flush/bypass must be understood and used correctly.","Anaesthesia workstation ले medical gas आपूर्ति, flow नियन्त्रण, आवश्यकताअनुसार vaporiser बाट volatile agent र breathing system मा gas पठाउँछ। Pipeline/cylinder, pressure, flowmeter, oxygen analyser, alarm, vaporiser, breathing circuit, leak test र ventilator checklist अनुसार जाँच्नुपर्छ।"],
 ["22. Airway devices, oxygenation and monitoring","Airway devices include oral/nasal airways, supraglottic devices, endotracheal tubes and tracheostomy tubes. Correct size, placement and secure fixation are essential. Pulse oximetry estimates peripheral oxygen saturation; capnography measures exhaled CO2 and helps confirm ventilation and tube placement. ECG, non-invasive BP, temperature and other monitors are selected according to patient and procedure. A manual resuscitator must be available and checked.","Airway device मा oral/nasal airway, supraglottic device, endotracheal tube र tracheostomy tube पर्छन्। सही size, placement र fixation आवश्यक हुन्छ। Pulse oximeter ले oxygen saturation अनुमान गर्छ; capnography ले निस्केको CO2 मापन गरी ventilation र tube position पुष्टि गर्न मद्दत गर्छ।"],
 ["23. Pre-operative assessment and preparation","Pre-operative preparation confirms identity, procedure, consent, fasting status, allergies, medicines, comorbidities, airway assessment, previous anaesthesia problems, investigations and blood availability where indicated. Consent is a process of informed voluntary decision-making by the patient or authorised decision-maker. NPO instructions depend on current guideline and patient factors; do not apply one fasting interval to every situation.","Pre-operative तयारीमा पहिचान, procedure, consent, fasting, allergy, औषधि, पुराना रोग, airway, पहिलेको anaesthesia समस्या, जाँच र आवश्यकताअनुसार रगत उपलब्धता पुष्टि हुन्छ। Consent भनेको जानकारी पाएपछि स्वेच्छाले निर्णय गर्ने प्रक्रिया हो। NPO निर्देशन हालको guideline र बिरामीअनुसार हुन्छ।"],
 ["24. Induction, intubation and maintenance","Anaesthesia induction requires a prepared patient, checked workstation, monitoring, IV access and a planned airway strategy. Intubation requires appropriate laryngoscope and tube selection, visualisation, atraumatic passage, cuff management and confirmation using sustained waveform capnography where available, alongside clinical checks. Secure the tube and reassess after movement. Maintenance includes anaesthetic delivery, analgesia, ventilation, haemodynamic monitoring, temperature, fluid/blood and electrolyte management.","Anaesthesia induction अघि बिरामी, workstation, monitoring, IV access र airway योजना तयार हुनुपर्छ। Intubation मा उपयुक्त laryngoscope र tube छान्ने, सावधानीपूर्वक राख्ने, cuff व्यवस्थापन र उपलब्ध भए waveform capnography सहित पुष्टि गर्ने। Tube सुरक्षित बाँधेर movement पछि पुनः जाँच्नुपर्छ।"],
 ["25. Patient positioning, protection and IV access","Positioning must provide surgical access while maintaining airway security, ventilation, circulation and nerve protection. Protect eyes, ears, skin, lips, tongue, teeth, veins, arteries and peripheral nerves. IV access requires vein assessment, aseptic preparation, appropriate cannula and secure fixation. Difficult access should be escalated early; avoid repeated traumatic attempts.","Positioning ले surgery का लागि पहुँच दिनुपर्छ तर airway, ventilation, circulation र nerve सुरक्षित राख्नुपर्छ। आँखा, कान, छाला, ओठ, जिब्रो, दाँत, vein, artery र peripheral nerve जोगाउनुपर्छ। IV cannulation मा vein जाँच, aseptic तयारी, उपयुक्त cannula र fixation चाहिन्छ।"],
 ["26. Emergence, extubation and post-anaesthesia recovery","Emergence includes reducing or stopping anaesthetic agents, assessing return of protective reflexes, reversing neuromuscular blockade when indicated, suctioning when needed and deciding on safe extubation. Recovery handover includes identity, procedure, anaesthesia, airway, drugs, fluids/blood, estimated losses, complications, analgesia, nausea plan and ongoing monitoring. Watch for airway obstruction, hypoventilation, hypoxia, haemodynamic instability, pain, nausea, agitation and delayed emergence.","Emergence मा anaesthetic घटाउने/रोक्ने, protective reflex फर्केको मूल्याङ्कन, आवश्यकताअनुसार neuromuscular blockade reversal, suction र सुरक्षित extubation निर्णय पर्छ। Recovery handover मा पहिचान, surgery, anaesthesia, airway, औषधि, fluid/blood, समस्या र monitoring जानकारी दिनुपर्छ।"],
 ["27. Applied and advanced anaesthesia: co-existing disease","Diabetes, hypertension, IHD, heart failure, arrhythmias, COPD/asthma, renal and liver disease, obesity, thyroid disorders, epilepsy, pregnancy, older age and paediatric/neonatal status change perioperative risk. Assessment should identify disease severity, functional status, medication, organ impairment and optimisation needs. Anaesthetic plans are individualised by the responsible anaesthesia team; the technologist supports preparation, equipment, monitoring and escalation.","Diabetes, hypertension, IHD, heart failure, arrhythmia, COPD/asthma, kidney/liver रोग, obesity, thyroid, epilepsy, pregnancy, वृद्ध र बाल/नवजात अवस्थाले perioperative जोखिम बदल्छ। रोगको गम्भीरता, औषधि, अंगको अवस्था र optimisation आवश्यकता पहिचान गर्नुपर्छ।"],
 ["28. Regional, spinal, epidural and local anaesthesia","Regional anaesthesia blocks nerve transmission in a defined region. Spinal anaesthesia delivers local anaesthetic into CSF; epidural anaesthesia delivers medication into the epidural space. Peripheral nerve blocks target selected nerves or plexuses. Local anaesthetic systemic toxicity, high/total spinal block, hypotension, bleeding, infection and nerve injury are important risks. Follow aseptic technique, monitoring and emergency readiness.","Regional anaesthesia ले निश्चित क्षेत्रमा nerve signal रोक्छ। Spinal मा CSF भित्र र epidural मा epidural space मा औषधि दिइन्छ। Peripheral nerve block ले छानिएका nerve/plexus मा काम गर्छ। Local anaesthetic toxicity, high spinal, hypotension, bleeding, infection र nerve injury महत्त्वपूर्ण जोखिम हुन्।"],
 ["29. Obstetric, paediatric, neonatal, thoracic and cardiac anaesthesia","Obstetric anaesthesia includes labour epidural analgesia, anaesthesia for LSCS and management considerations in pre-eclampsia. Paediatric and neonatal patients differ in airway size, physiology, drug handling and temperature regulation. Newborn resuscitation requires current neonatal life-support guidance. Thoracic and cardiac procedures require advanced planning for ventilation, haemodynamics, perfusion and postoperative care under specialist teams.","Obstetric anaesthesia मा labour epidural, LSCS र pre-eclampsia व्यवस्थापन पर्छ। बाल तथा नवजात बिरामीमा airway, physiology, औषधि metabolism र तापक्रम नियन्त्रण फरक हुन्छ। Newborn resuscitation मा हालको neonatal life-support guideline पालना गर्नुपर्छ।"],
 ["30. Ventilation, PFT and critical events","Pulmonary function tests help assess airflow obstruction, restriction and respiratory reserve. Ventilators support or control ventilation using different modes; settings must be individualised and monitored. Humidification and aerosol therapy support selected respiratory care. Shock, low cardiac output and cardiac arrest require rapid recognition, emergency activation, CPR/advanced support by trained teams and continuous reassessment.","Pulmonary function test ले airflow obstruction, restriction र respiratory reserve मूल्याङ्कन गर्छ। Ventilator ले विभिन्न mode बाट ventilation सहयोग वा नियन्त्रण गर्छ; setting बिरामीअनुसार मिलाएर निगरानी गर्नुपर्छ। Shock, low cardiac output र cardiac arrest छिटो पहिचान गरी प्रशिक्षित टोलीबाट emergency response आवश्यक हुन्छ।"]
 ];
